61-0-0","condition":"stage C, the first time you step inside the door. Elm talks to you. The boy and girl versions are the same except one line: a boy player probably hears \"Just like your friend Lyra does!\", a girl player \"Just like your friend Ethan does!\".","stages":["C"],"ids":["NBT-DLG-061-12b","NBT-DLG-061-12f","NBT-DLG-061-12c","NBT-DLG-061-12d","NBT-DLG-061-12e"],"blocks":[{"type":"dialogue","text":"Professor Elm: Hi, [Player]!\nI’ve been waiting for you!\n\nDo you know anything about\nmy research?\n\nAs you know, Pokémon are carried\nin Poké Balls these days.\n\nBut before the Poké Ball was invented,\npeople used to walk with Pokémon.\n\nJust like your friend Lyra does!\n\nPoké Balls are great because you can\ncarry many Pokémon.\n\nBut walking with Pokémon must have\nsome advantages.\n\nIt could have something to do with how\nPokémon grow or evolve...\n\nSo I’m going to give you a Pokémon!\n\nCan you walk beside this Pokémon,\noutside of its Poké Ball, to see if this\n\nbrings any special feelings or bonds\n\nbetween Pokémon and people?\n\nThe device over there has some Pokémon\nyou could choose from...","id":"61-0-0-block-0","gender":"male"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Professor Elm: Hi, [Player]!\nI’ve been waiting for you!\n\nDo you know anything about\nmy research?\n\nAs you know, Pokémon are carried\nin Poké Balls these days.\n\nBut before the Poké Ball was invented,\npeople used to walk with Pokémon.\n\nJust like your friend Ethan does!\n\nPoké Balls are great because you can\ncarry many Pokémon.\n\nBut walking with Pokémon must have\nsome advantages.\n\nIt could have something to do with how\nPokémon grow or evolve...\n\nSo I’m going to give you a Pokémon!\n\nCan you walk beside this Pokémon,\noutside of its Poké Ball, to see if this\n\nbrings any special feelings or bonds\n\nbetween Pokémon and people?\n\nThe device over there has some Pokémon\nyou could choose from...","id":"61-0-0-block-0-female","gender":"female"},{"type":"note","text":"Then Elm gets an email.","id":"61-0-0-block-1","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Professor Elm: Oh, hey! I got an email!","id":"61-0-0-block-2","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Professor Elm: ...\nHm... Uh-huh... OK...","id":"61-0-0-block-3","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Professor Elm: Hey, listen.\nI have this acquaintance that people\n\ncall Mr. Pokémon.\n\nHe keeps finding weird things and\nraving about his discoveries.\n\nAnyway, I just got an email from him\nsaying that this time it’s real.\n\nIt’s probably another Pokémon Egg,\nbut we’re still so busy with our\n\nPokémon research...\n\nWait!\nI know!\n\nYou can go in our place, right?\nCan we count on you?\n\nYou can choose one of the Pokémon\nover there.","id":"61-0-0-block-4","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"After this you can walk around, but you cannot leave the lab yet.","id":"61-0-0-block-5","gender":"both"}],"uncertain":true,"evidence":[{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-12b","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"Elm","trigger":"trigger 1; male","condition":"flag 352 clear, var 0x4108=0","source":"843 F#21,#66; 543 m0"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-12f","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"Elm","trigger":"trigger 1; female","condition":"as 12b","source":"843 F#21,#66; 543 m1"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-12c","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"Elm","trigger":"trigger 1, phone ring","condition":"as 12b","source":"843 F#21,#66; 543 m2"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-12d","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"Elm","trigger":"trigger 1, after 12c","condition":"as 12b","source":"843 F#21,#66; 543 m3"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-12e","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"Elm","trigger":"trigger 1, after Elm steps","condition":"as 12b","source":"843 F#21,#66; 543 m4"}]}],"kind":"element","gender":"both","legacyNames":["Scene when you first walk into the lab"]},{"id":"61-1","name":"Trying To Leave Before You Choose A Pokémon","events":["NBT-EVT-061-12"],"context":"[NBT-EVT-061-12]\n\n","points":[{"id":"61-1-0","condition":"stage C, after Elm's welcome, when you walk to the door again.","stages":["C"],"ids":["NBT-DLG-061-12a"],"blocks":[{"type":"dialogue","text":"Professor Elm: Where are you going?\nThe Poké Balls are in that device.","id":"61-1-0-block-0","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"You are moved one step back from the door.","id":"61-1-0-block-1","gender":"both"}],"uncertain":false,"evidence":[{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-12a","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"Elm","trigger":"trigger 1 (F#19)","condition":"flag 352 set, var 0x4108=0","source":"843 F#19; 543 m6"}]}],"kind":"element","gender":"both","legacyNames":["Trying to leave before you choose a Pokémon"]},{"id":"61-2","name":"The Machine With The Poké Balls","events":["NBT-EVT-061-13"],"context":"[NBT-EVT-061-13]\n\n","points":[{"id":"61-2-0","condition":"stage C, the first time you check the machine. A screen lets you choose Chikorita, Cyndaquil or Totodile. After you pick:","stages":["C"],"ids":["NBT-DLG-061-13a","NBT-DLG-061-13b","NBT-DLG-061-13c","NBT-DLG-061-13d","NBT-DLG-061-13e"],"blocks":[{"type":"dialogue","text":"[Player] received [Pokémon]\nfrom Professor Elm!","id":"61-2-0-block-0","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"Then you are asked about a nickname.","id":"61-2-0-block-1","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Give a nickname to the [Pokémon]\nyou received?","id":"61-2-0-block-2","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"You are asked Yes or No. Yes: the naming screen opens, then you are asked to confirm. No: no nickname.","id":"61-2-0-block-3","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Is [Nickname] the nickname\nyou want to give?","id":"61-2-0-block-4","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"You are asked Yes or No. Yes keeps the name. No opens the naming screen again.","id":"61-2-0-block-5","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"Then Elm speaks while your new Pokémon walks beside you. After this he gives you directions to Mr. Pokémon (his stage D line, under \"Professor Elm\" below), and you can leave the lab.","id":"61-2-0-block-6","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Professor Elm: How do you like walking\nwith your Pokémon? It’s not bad, is it?\n\nYou can take it all the way to\nMr. Pokémon’s house.\n\nIf your Pokémon gets hurt...","id":"61-2-0-block-7","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"You should heal it with this machine.\n\nIt’s so easy to use.\nJust check the PC on my desk!","id":"61-2-0-block-8","gender":"both"}],"uncertain":false,"evidence":[{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-13a","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"narration","trigger":"machine, flag 106 clear","condition":"flag 106 clear","source":"843 S#13; 543 m7"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-13b","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"narration","trigger":"nickname prompt","condition":"flag 106 clear path","source":"843 S#13; 543 m8"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-13c","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"narration","trigger":"nickname confirm","condition":"after name screen","source":"843 F#23; 543 m9"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-13d","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"Elm","trigger":"after nickname step","condition":"same run","source":"843 S#13; 543 m10"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-13e","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"Elm","trigger":"after 13d","condition":"same run","source":"843 S#13; 543 m11"}]},{"id":"61-2-1","condition":"you check the machine again after you have your Pokémon, before you have Falkner's TM from the Violet City Gym, and before a certain event in Cherrygrove (the game's own label for it mentions meeting a passer-by).","stages":[],"ids":["NBT-DLG-061-13f"],"blocks":[{"type":"dialogue","text":"There are two valuable Pokémon left!\n...But they belong to Professor Elm.","id":"61-2-1-block-0","gender":"both"}],"uncertain":false,"evidence":[{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-13f","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"machine narration","trigger":"machine (F#22)","condition":"flag 106 set, 115 and 153 clear","source":"843 F#22; 543 m15"}]},{"id":"61-2-2","condition":"the same, but after that Cherrygrove event.","stages":[],"ids":["NBT-DLG-061-13g"],"blocks":[{"type":"dialogue","text":"There is one valuable Pokémon left!\nYou didn’t notice before, but it is\n\nbehind thick glass walls now so\n\nnothing bad can happen to it!","id":"61-2-2-block-0","gender":"both"}],"uncertain":false,"evidence":[{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-13g","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"machine narration","trigger":"machine (F#53)","condition":"flag 106 set, 115 clear, 153 set","source":"843 F#53; 543 m16"}]},{"id":"61-2-3","condition":"after you have Falkner's TM from the Violet City Gym.","stages":[],"ids":["NBT-DLG-061-13h"],"blocks":[{"type":"dialogue","text":"There are no valuable Pokémon left...\n\nYou wonder who Professor Elm gave the\nlast Pokémon to?","id":"61-2-3-block-0","gender":"both"}],"uncertain":false,"evidence":[{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-13h","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"machine narration","trigger":"machine (F#52)","condition":"flag 106 set, 115 set","source":"843 F#52; 543 m17"}]}],"kind":"element","gender":"both","legacyNames":["The machine with the Poké Balls"]},{"id":"61-3","name":"The Aide Stops You At The Door (Items For Your Errand)","events":["NBT-EVT-061-04"],"context":"[NBT-EVT-061-04]\n\n","points":[{"id":"61-3-0","condition":"stage D, when you walk towards the door with your first Pokémon. The aide walks over to you. Boy and girl players hear the same words.","stages":["D"],"ids":["NBT-DLG-061-04a","NBT-DLG-061-04c","NBT-DLG-061-04b"],"blocks":[{"type":"dialogue","text":"[Player], I want you to have these\nto help you with your task.","id":"61-3-0-block-0","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"You receive five Potions. If your Bag is full, you get nothing, and this happens again the next time you walk to the door. If certain game-mode options were chosen at the start, he also gives a Rare Candy, Premier Ball, Max Repel and Escape Rope, or every key item, or a Porygon.","id":"61-3-0-block-1","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Pokémon are weak in the beginning.\n\nDon’t hesitate to use a Potion if you\nthink yours is in danger.","id":"61-3-0-block-2","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"The aide walks back to his place.","id":"61-3-0-block-3","gender":"both"}],"uncertain":false,"evidence":[{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-04a","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"aide","trigger":"trigger 0; male","condition":"var 0x4108=1","source":"843 F#15,#64; 543 m19"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-04c","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"aide","trigger":"trigger 0; female","condition":"var 0x4108=1","source":"843 F#15,#64; 543 m20"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-04b","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"aide","trigger":"after items given","condition":"handout succeeded","source":"843 F#15,#64; 543 m21"}]}],"kind":"element","gender":"both","legacyNames":["The aide stops you at the door (items for your errand)"]},{"id":"61-4","name":"The Healing PC On Elm's Desk","events":["NBT-EVT-061-14"],"context":"[NBT-EVT-061-14]\n\n","points":[{"id":"61-4-0","condition":"you check it before you have a Pokémon.","stages":[],"ids":["NBT-DLG-061-14a"],"blocks":[{"type":"dialogue","text":"This PC is connected to the\nhealing machine!","id":"61-4-0-block-0","gender":"both"}],"uncertain":false,"evidence":[{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-14a","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"PC narration","trigger":"PC","condition":"flag 106 clear","source":"843 F#24; 543 m14"}]},{"id":"61-4-1","condition":"you check it once you have a Pokémon.","stages":[],"ids":["NBT-DLG-061-14b"],"blocks":[{"type":"dialogue","text":"Would you like to heal\nyour Pokémon?","id":"61-4-1-block-0","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"You are asked Yes or No. Yes: the screen fades, a jingle plays and your Pokémon are healed. No: nothing happens.","id":"61-4-1-block-1","gender":"both"}],"uncertain":false,"evidence":[{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-14b","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"PC narration","trigger":"PC Yes/No","condition":"flag 106 set","source":"843 S#14; 543 m92"}]}],"kind":"element","gender":"both","legacyNames":["The healing PC on Elm's desk"]},{"id":"61-5","name":"Scene When You Come Back From The Errand","events":["NBT-EVT-061-03"],"context":"[NBT-EVT-061-03]\n\n","points":[{"id":"61-5-0","condition":"stage F, the first time you walk into the lab after visiting Mr. Pokémon. You are walked in and an officer turns to you.","stages":["F"],"ids":["NBT-DLG-061-03a","NBT-DLG-061-03b","NBT-DLG-061-03m","NBT-DLG-061-03c","NBT-DLG-061-03d","NBT-DLG-061-03e","NBT-DLG-061-03f","NBT-DLG-061-03g","NBT-DLG-061-03n","NBT-DLG-061-03h","NBT-DLG-061-03o","NBT-DLG-061-03i","NBT-DLG-061-03j","NBT-DLG-061-03k","NBT-DLG-061-03p","NBT-DLG-061-03l","NBT-DLG-061-03q"],"blocks":[{"type":"dialogue","text":"Who are you?\nWe are investigating the case of the\n\nmissing Pokémon here...\n\nRule number one!\n\"Whoever did it will come\n\nback to the site.\"\n\nOh my... So you must be...\nthe one who did it?","id":"61-5-0-block-0","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"Your friend runs in.","id":"61-5-0-block-1","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"(boy player, probably)","id":"61-5-0-block-2","gender":"male"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Lyra: Hold on a second!\nHe has nothing to do with it!\n\nI saw it.\nThere was a red-haired boy\n\nlooking into the building!","id":"61-5-0-block-3","gender":"male"},{"type":"note","text":"(girl player, probably)","id":"61-5-0-block-4","gender":"female"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Ethan: Hold on a second!\nShe has nothing to do with it!\n\nI saw it.\nThere was a red-haired boy\n\nlooking into the building!","id":"61-5-0-block-5","gender":"female"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"What?\nYou battled a boy like that?\n\nHe must be the one who did it...\nDid you happen to get his name?","id":"61-5-0-block-6","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"The naming screen opens and you type your rival's name.","id":"61-5-0-block-7","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"I see! So [Rival] was\nhis name.","id":"61-5-0-block-8","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"You are asked Yes or No. Yes: the officer thanks you and leaves. No: he asks again and the naming screen reopens, until you say Yes.","id":"61-5-0-block-9","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Thanks for helping my investigation!\n\nMy next assignment is to search for\nthis red-haired individual.","id":"61-5-0-block-10","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"If you said No:","id":"61-5-0-block-11","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"That’s not it?\n\nThen can you tell me\nwhat the name was?","id":"61-5-0-block-12","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"After the officer leaves, your friend speaks and walks out. Boy and girl players hear the same words except the name: Lyra for a boy player, Ethan for a girl player (probably).","id":"61-5-0-block-13","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Lyra: [Player]!\nI’m glad they understand you are\n\ninnocent.\n\nSee you later!","id":"61-5-0-block-14","gender":"male"},{"type":"note","text":"Elm turns to you. The Mystery Egg is taken from your Bag. Boy and girl players hear the same words.","id":"61-5-0-block-15","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Professor Elm: [Player], this\nis terrible...\n\nOh, yes, what was Mr. Pokémon’s\nbig discovery?","id":"61-5-0-block-16","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"[Player] handed the Mystery Egg\nto Professor Elm.","id":"61-5-0-block-17","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Professor Elm: Huh?\nThis is an...Egg, isn’t it?\n\nThis Egg may be something I’ve never\nseen...still it’s just an Egg.\n\nMr. Pokémon is always fascinated\nby Eggs.\n\nWell, since he gave it to us, we might\nas well find out what secret it holds.\n\nI’ll keep it for a while to find out\nabout the Egg.","id":"61-5-0-block-18","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"Professor Elm: What?!\n\nProfessor Oak gave you a Pokédex?\n\n[Player], is that true? Th-that’s\nincredible!\n\nHe is superb at seeing the potential\nof people as Trainers.\n\nWow, [Player].\nI knew you were a little different.\n\nThings are going to be fun!\n\nYour Pokémon seem to really like you,\nso why don’t you...take the\n\nPokémon Gym challenge?\n\nIf you manage to defeat all the\nGym Leaders, you’ll eventually\n\nchallenge the Pokémon League\n\nChampion!\n\n...Or not! Ha ha!\n\nBecoming the Champion is not at all\neasy, but you can certainly\n\nchallenge Violet City’s Gym.","id":"61-5-0-block-19","gender":"both"},{"type":"dialogue","text":"...[Player]. Challenging the\nGyms scattered around will be\n\na long journey.\n\nBefore you leave, make sure\nthat you talk to your mom.","id":"61-5-0-block-20","gender":"both"},{"type":"note","text":"The scene plays once.","id":"61-5-0-block-21","gender":"both"}],"uncertain":false,"evidence":[{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-03a","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"officer ow1","trigger":"scene","condition":"var 0x4108=3","source":"843 S#3; 543 m23"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-03b","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"friend \"Lyra\"","trigger":"scene; male","condition":"var 0x4108=3","source":"843 S#3; 543 m24"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-03m","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"friend \"Ethan\"","trigger":"scene; female","condition":"var 0x4108=3","source":"843 S#3; 543 m25"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-03c","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"officer","trigger":"scene, before naming screen","condition":"var 0x4108=3","source":"843 S#3; 543 m26"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-03d","type":"Dialogue variant","area":"61 Elm lab","speaker":"officer","trigger":"name confirm Yes/No","condition":"var 0x4108=3","source":"843 S#3,F#12; 543 m27"},{"id":"NBT-DLG-061-03e","type"